# The linker written onto a numeral from eleven upward, which puts the counted
# noun back in the singular ("ħdax-il jum", "tlettax-il raġel").  The
# tokenizer shears the hyphen, so it arrives as its own token and the counted
# orders take it as an optional connector.  en.wiktionary.org,
# Module:number_list/data/mt ("Numbers 11-19 use the suffix -il in construct
# forms"); malteseforbeginners.blogspot.com, "The Numbers (In-Numri)".
il
